# Product Skill Routing

Use this rule when the user asks to create, generate, review, export, or refine presentation deck artifacts in this repository.

Canonical source: `skills/*.md`

MUST:

- Route product-skill requests to the canonical skill document first.
- Keep `.claude/commands/*.md` and `.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md` as tool-specific wrappers, not the source of truth.
- Follow gates in the canonical skill document. Do not skip user confirmation gates for speed.
- For PPTX/PDF/preview generation, use the npm scripts documented by the skill.

| User intent | Canonical skill |
| --- | --- |
| Create a presentation, deck, PPT, or write a blueprint | `skills/create-deck.md` |
| Review a deck, PPTX, preview, or blueprint | `skills/review-deck.md` |
| Export a PPTX to PDF | `skills/export-pdf.md` |
| Generate an architecture slide diagram spec | `skills/generate-architecture-slide.md` |
| Create a custom design preset from brand assets | `skills/customize-preset.md` |

Notes:

- Cursor does not use the Claude Code slash-command wrappers directly.
- `customize-preset` is currently a documented/reference skill. Treat it as guidance unless a dedicated wrapper or validated end-to-end workflow is added.
